;; The absorbed-uses sweep of `rebuild_congruence` reactivates a collapsed node it
;; recanonicalizes, so a class's stored minimal monomial is never a collapsed node (I5).
;; The merge `C3 = C4` turns a collapsed node and an active node of one class into the
;; same monomial `c³`. The collapsed one was the stored minimal monomial; the sweep kept
;; its flag, and the refresh of the active copy kept the stored one (equal, not less), so
;; the debug check `check_min_monomial_invariant` failed: "stored minimal monomial ... is
;; collapsed". Cancellation gives `C1 = C3` from `c1c3 = c3²` and then `C2 = C3`.
;; Expected: ok. Reduced from `semper-conform-cc-cert` seed 911, case 985.
(sort E)
(function C0 () E)
(function C1 () E)
(function C2 () E)
(function C3 () E)
(function C4 () E)
(function Add (E) E :assoc-comm :cancellative)
(set-option :completion eager)
(union (Add (C1) (C3)) (Add (C4):2))
(union (Add (C3):2 (C4):2) (C3))
(union (Add (C1) (C3):2) (Add (C2) (C3):2))
(union (C3) (C4))
(check-eq (C1) (C3))
(check-eq (C2) (C3))
(check-eq (Add (C3):4) (C3))
